# A missing hashed asset must be a REAL 404 — never the SPA fallback. Serving
# index.html (200, text/html) under an /assets/*.js URL is what poisoned
# browsers/edge during deploy races (the _headers immutable rule keys on the
# URL, so the HTML got cached for a year under the chunk's address — Jul 27/28
# incidents). 404.html ships with Cache-Control: no-cache, so a mid-deploy miss
# is retried cleanly by guard.js instead of being cached forever.
/assets/* /404.html 404

# SPA fallback: every other path serves the app shell; the client router takes over
/* /index.html 200
